; The one variable: WHICH stages `StyleBoxFlat::draw` runs — `skew` and the drop
; shadow. Every other stylebox scene varies the ring it already draws (radii,
; border widths, blend); neither field here changes a radius or a width, so a
; regression in either is invisible in all of them. Four Panels, same 480x260
; rect and fill, over a backdrop light enough to measure a fade against.
;
; SkewSharp — sharp corners, horizontal skew only. Ignore `skew` and you draw an
; axis-aligned rectangle, so the whole silhouette moves. Also the only place a
; golden exercises the second half of `aa_on`
; (`rounded_corners || !skew.is_zero_approx()`): a sharp box that still feathers.
; SkewRound — skew on both axes plus a border, proving every ring shears about
; ONE centre; per-ring centres detach the border from the fill.
; ShadowOffset — shadow down-right, no border, so shadow and box are separable
; by eye. `shadow_size` 24 because a small fade reads as a feather.
; ShadowHollow — shadow plus `draw_center = false`, so the shadow is a ring too
; and the backdrop shows through both; offset UP-LEFT so a sign error fails one.
;
; Measured against Godot 4.6.3 at `--mode 2d`: whole-frame mean channel error
; 0.19, nothing past 6 counts. Nearly all of the mean is one count of green on
; the fill (0.3 x 255 = 76.5, the reference's ROP floor); the rest is SkewRound's
; doubly-sheared edges.

